# The dummy application's generated files.
#
# Both patterns are needed, for the same reason: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to the
# directory holding the .gitignore, so `db/*.sqlite3` and `log/*.log` above match only the repo
# root's db/ and log/ and never reach test/dummy.  (rails-8.0.x spells the second one `log/`,
# with no slash, which *does* match a log directory at any depth -- hence the difference between
# the branches, and hence an earlier version of this comment being wrong about it here.)
#
# Adding the patterns is not enough on its own either: .gitignore is never consulted for a path
# already in the index, so these needed a `git rm --cached` as well.
test/dummy/db/*.sqlite3
test/dummy/log/*.log
